<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-CBA says CFM fully integrated.</title>
<headline>RTRS-CBA says CFM fully integrated.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Commonwealth Bank of Australia (CBA) said on Thursday it had completed the integration of Commonwealth Funds Management (CFM) in its funds management arm, Commonwealth Financial Services.</p>
<p>&quot;All funds management activity will be consolidated under Shaun Mays, recently appointed chief investment officer,&quot; CBA said.</p>
<p>CFS would keep CFM's retail business in Canberra to stay close to its public servant clients. These operations would be headed by John Jones, previously CFM's manager of retail operations.  </p>
<p>The Australian government announced in December last year that CBA was the preferred buyer for CFM.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
